    "html": "\n<p><strong>Last updated: 19 November 2026.</strong></p>\n<p>UPSC will hold the Civil Services Examination 2026 Personality Tests (interviews) for 2,526 candidates from Monday, 7 December 2026 to 12 February 2027, according to the Commission's official notice dated 17 November 2026.</p>\n\n<div class=\"tldr-box\"><p class=\"tldr-label\">Quick facts</p>\n<p><strong>Interviews:</strong> 7 December 2026 to 12 February 2027, at UPSC, Dholpur House, Shahjahan Road, New Delhi</p>\n<p><strong>Candidates called:</strong> 2,526, listed by roll number, date and session in the official PDF</p>\n<p><strong>Reporting time:</strong> 9:00 am for the forenoon session, 1:00 pm for the afternoon session</p>\n<p><strong>Online details window:</strong> 11 November to 25 November 2026, until 6:00 pm; no e-summon letter if you miss it</p>\n<p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Intv-CSM-2026-Engl-171126.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UPSC important notice, 17 Nov 2026</a></p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>What UPSC has announced</h2>\n<p>The Commission's <a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Intv-CSM-2026-Engl-171126.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">important notice</a>, posted on its <a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/whats-new/Civil%20Services%20%28Main%29%20Examination%2C%202026/Interview%20Schedule\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">What's New page</a>, says Personality Tests for the Civil Services (Main) Examination 2026 will begin on Monday, 7 December 2026. The notice follows the Mains written result that UPSC declared on 5 November 2026.</p>\n<p>The PDF lists all 2,526 candidates who qualified for the Personality Test, with each roll number given an interview date and a forenoon or afternoon session. The schedule runs from 7 December 2026 to 12 February 2027. Reporting time is 9:00 am for the forenoon session and 1:00 pm for the afternoon session.</p>\n<p>UPSC has added a firm condition. Any candidate who does not fill up or update the required details online between 11 November and 25 November 2026 (till 6:00 pm) will not get an e-summon letter and will not be allowed to appear in the interview.</p>\n<p>The notice says e-summon letters will be made available shortly on upsc.gov.in and upsconline.nic.in. It also says requests to change the date or time of an interview will ordinarily not be entertained.</p>\n<p>On travel costs, the notice says reimbursement is limited to second-class or sleeper-class train fare by mail or express trains. Candidates must submit ticket copies for both ways along with the TA claim form in duplicate, available on UPSC's <a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/forms-downloads\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">forms and downloads page</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>What it means for candidates</h2>\n<p>If you cleared Mains, your first job is to finish the online details form before 6:00 pm on 25 November. That deadline is six days away, and missing it costs you the interview itself.</p>\n<p>Next, find your roll number in the PDF and note your exact date and session. With interviews spread over about ten weeks, some candidates have less than three weeks to prepare and others have nearly three months. Plan your mock interviews around your own date, not the start date.</p>\n<p>Keep your Detailed Application Form handy. Interview boards usually build questions around your home state, education, hobbies and service preferences, so re-read what you filled in.</p>\n<p>If you are travelling to Delhi, book train tickets early, particularly for dates near Christmas and New Year, and keep both tickets for the TA claim.</p>\n\n<h2>Important pointers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>19 Nov 2026:</strong> UPSC CSE 2026 interviews run from 7 December 2026 to 12 February 2027 for 2,526 candidates, per UPSC's notice dated 17 November 2026 (<a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Intv-CSM-2026-Engl-171126.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UPSC notice</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>19 Nov 2026:</strong> CSE 2026 interview candidates who do not submit their details online by 6:00 pm on 25 November 2026 will not get an e-summon letter and cannot appear (<a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Intv-CSM-2026-Engl-171126.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UPSC notice</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>19 Nov 2026:</strong> The Indian Forest Service (Main) Examination 2026 runs from 22 to 29 November 2026, with no paper on 24 November, a gazetted holiday (<a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/TT-IFSM-26-Engl-170926.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UPSC IFoS Mains time-table</a>); e-admit cards are on the UPSC website (<a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/content/e-admit-cards-ifos-main-examination-2026\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UPSC notice</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>19 Nov 2026:</strong> UPSC's Annual Calendar 2027 sets the Civil Services (Preliminary) Examination 2027 for 23 May 2027, with the notification due on 13 January 2027 and applications closing on 2 February 2027 (<a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Calendar-Year-2027-Engl-200526.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UPSC Annual Calendar 2027</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>19 Nov 2026:</strong> The NDA &amp; NA (I) and CDS (I) 2027 notification is due on 2 December 2026, with applications closing on 22 December 2026 and the exam on 11 April 2027, per UPSC's Annual Calendar 2027 (<a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Calendar-Year-2027-Engl-200526.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UPSC Annual Calendar 2027</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Preparing for UPSC or GPSC in Gujarat? See our new city guide, <a href=\"top-ias-coaching-institutes-gandhinagar-2026.html\">Top IAS Coaching Institutes in Gandhinagar</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Last updated: 19 November 2026.</strong></p>\n"
