    "html": "\n<p><strong>Last updated: 19 November 2026.</strong></p>\n<p>Gandhinagar, Gujarat's capital and the seat of the Gujarat Public Service Commission, has three UPSC coaching options we could confirm on their own official websites: DICS and Chahal Academy in Kudasan, and the Centre of Continuing Education at Pandit Deendayal Energy University (PDEU). This guide lists only what we could confirm, and says what we could not.</p>\n\n<div class=\"tldr-box\"><p class=\"tldr-label\">Quick facts</p>\n<p><strong>City:</strong> Gandhinagar, Gujarat</p>\n<p><strong>Exams covered:</strong> UPSC Civil Services and GPSC Class 1 and 2</p>\n<p><strong>Institutes listed:</strong> 3, each checked on its own official website on 19 November 2026</p>\n<p><strong>Coaching area:</strong> Kudasan, on the Gandhinagar side of the Ahmedabad border</p>\n<p><strong>Published fees:</strong> Rs 95,000 to Rs 1,95,000 for multi-year UPSC or UPSC plus GPSC programmes at the two private institutes</p>\n<p><strong>GPSC office:</strong> Sector 10-A, near Chh-3 Circle, Gandhinagar 382010 (<a href=\"https://gpsc.gujarat.gov.in/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">gpsc.gujarat.gov.in</a>)</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Why Gandhinagar matters for civil services aspirants</h2>\n<p>Gandhinagar is home to the Gujarat secretariat and the <a href=\"https://gpsc.gujarat.gov.in/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Gujarat Public Service Commission</a>, which recruits for Gujarat Administrative Service and other Class 1 and 2 posts. Many aspirants here write both UPSC CSE and the GPSC exams, so institutes in the city tend to offer a combined UPSC plus GPSC track with Gujarat-specific papers.</p>\n<p>The city also sits next to Ahmedabad, Gujarat's largest coaching market. Students from north Gujarat often choose Gandhinagar for a quieter study base with Ahmedabad's libraries and test centres a short drive away.</p>\n<p>The calendar is also turning. UPSC's <a href=\"https://www.upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Calendar-Year-2027-Engl-200526.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Annual Calendar 2027</a> sets CSE Prelims 2027 for 23 May 2027, with the notification due on 13 January 2027. New foundation batches that start now leave about six months to prelims.</p>\n\n<h2>How we picked this list</h2>\n<p>We included an institute only if its own website shows UPSC or GPSC coaching at a Gandhinagar address. Directory sites name several more Gandhinagar classes, but without an official page we did not rank them. We kept the list to three instead of padding it to ten. Our paid listings get no extra ranking unless they qualify on the same test. If you run or know an institute that should be here, send us its official page and we will check it.</p>\n\n<h3>1. DICS, Kudasan</h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://dics.co/upsc-ias-ips-coaching-in-gandhinagar\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DICS Gandhinagar page</a> gives the branch address as A-306, The Landmark, Urjanagar-1, opposite Spicy Street, Kudasan-Por Road, Kudasan, Gandhinagar 382421. It lists UPSC GS prelims-cum-mains programmes of 14, 28 and 42 months, plus test series, answer writing and mock interviews, and a GPSC Class 1 and 2 foundation batch in Gujarati medium. Published UPSC fees run from Rs 95,000 (14 months, one-time payment) to Rs 1,80,000 (unlimited duration); the UPSC plus GPSC hybrid runs from Rs 1,05,000 to Rs 1,95,000. Batches are listed at 8 to 10 am, 3 to 5 pm and 5:45 to 7:45 pm. No founding year or Gandhinagar-specific results are published.</p>\n\n<h3>2. Chahal Academy, Kudasan</h3>\n<p>Chahal Academy's <a href=\"https://chahalacademy.com/best-ias-coaching-in-gandhinagar\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">official Gandhinagar page</a> gives the address as C 201/202, The Landmark, Pandit Dindayal Upadhyay Marg, Kudasan, Gandhinagar 382421, in the same complex as DICS. The page describes the centre as franchisee owned and operated. It lists offline UPSC batches from 8 to 10:30 am and 5 to 7:30 pm on weekdays, a weekend batch for working professionals, and fees of Rs 1,00,000 to Rs 1,80,000 depending on programme length. It also links to a GPSC course, but gives no GPSC fee. Results quoted on the page are for the brand as a whole, not this centre.</p>\n\n<h3>3. Centre of Continuing Education, PDEU, Raisan</h3>\n<p>Pandit Deendayal Energy University's <a href=\"https://pdeu.ac.in/cce\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Centre of Continuing Education page</a> describes UPSC Civil Services coaching for prelims, mains and interview, with sessions involving serving and retired civil servants. The centre's address is Raisan village, Gandhinagar 382007. The page gives no fees, batch dates or results, and parts of it still carry template text, so call the centre before planning around it. It does not mention GPSC coaching.</p>\n\n<h2>What we left out, and why</h2>\n<p>SPIPA, the Gujarat government's institute that runs subsidised UPSC training, lists a <a href=\"https://spipa.gujarat.gov.in/regional-training-centres\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Regional Training Centre in Gandhinagar</a>, but its official page describes that centre as a training unit for secretariat staff, not a UPSC coaching centre. SPIPA's UPSC classes are admission-by-entrance, and we found no official page placing a UPSC batch in Gandhinagar. Directory sites list other Gandhinagar names, including Civils IAS and Praajasv Foundation, but we found no official page confirming a current Gandhinagar batch and address for them.</p>\n\n<h2>How to choose</h2>\n<p>DICS and Chahal sit in the same Kudasan building, publish similar multi-year fee bands and both offer a GPSC track, so visit both on the same day and compare a demo class and the batch timing that fits your day. DICS publishes more detail on its GPSC and hybrid fees; Chahal offers a weekend batch for working aspirants. PDEU's centre suits students who want a university-run option, but its page gives too little detail to judge on paper.</p>\n<p>Whichever you pick, ask three questions before paying: how many students in your batch, who teaches the Gujarat-specific GPSC papers, and what the refund policy is if you drop out after prelims. See every verified listing in the city on our <a href=\"coaching-gandhinagar.html\">Gandhinagar coaching page</a>, and check this week's <a href=\"upsc-cse-2026-interview-schedule-7-december-to-12-february-2526-candidates-19nov-update.html\">UPSC CSE 2026 interview schedule</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Last updated: 19 November 2026.</strong></p>\n"
