    "html": "\n<p><strong>Last updated: 18 November 2026.</strong></p>\n<p>The Maharashtra State CET Cell has scheduled the first attempt of MAH MBA/MMS CET 2027 for 28 to 30 January 2027 and the second attempt for 1 to 3 April 2027, in a tentative schedule for the 2027-28 admission year dated 16 November 2026.</p>\n\n<div class=\"tldr-box\"><p class=\"tldr-label\">Quick facts</p>\n<p><strong>MBA/MMS CET 2027, attempt 1:</strong> 28 to 30 January 2027 (tentative)</p>\n<p><strong>MBA/MMS CET 2027, attempt 2:</strong> 1 to 3 April 2027 (tentative)</p>\n<p><strong>Courses in the MBA group:</strong> MBA, MMS, PGDM and PGCM</p>\n<p><strong>New this year:</strong> PGDM and PGCM admissions come under a CET for the first time</p>\n<p><strong>Registration dates:</strong> not announced yet</p>\n<p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://cetcell.mahacet.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/DATES-OF-COMMENCEMENT-OF-MAHA-CET-2027-16-NOV-2026.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">State CET Cell press note, 16.11.2026 (Marathi)</a>; <a href=\"https://cetcell.mahacet.org/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">cetcell.mahacet.org</a></p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>What the CET Cell has announced</h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://cetcell.mahacet.org/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Maharashtra State CET Cell</a> posted a press note on 16 November 2026 listing the dates on which entrance tests for the 2027-28 academic year will begin. The note is in Marathi and all dates in it are marked tentative.</p>\n<p>For the MBA group, the note lists MBA, MMS, PGDM and PGCM together. The first attempt is set for 28 to 30 January 2027 and the second attempt for 1 to 3 April 2027. The note says this is the first time a CET will be held for PGDM and PGCM courses, along with GNM nursing.</p>\n<p>The press note also states that the first CET is compulsory for students and the second attempt is optional. It does not give registration dates, fees or exam-centre details, which usually come in a separate information brochure.</p>\n<p>The same note lists dates for other Maharashtra CETs, including MCA, law, MHT CET and BBA/BCA. We have not reproduced those here because the PDF text is hard to read in places; check the <a href=\"https://cetcell.mahacet.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/DATES-OF-COMMENCEMENT-OF-MAHA-CET-2027-16-NOV-2026.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">official PDF</a> directly for those courses.</p>\n\n<h2>What it means for MBA aspirants</h2>\n<p>If you are writing CAT 2026 on 29 November, the first MBA CET attempt falls about two months later, after XAT (3 January) and before most IIM and state-college interview calls. That gives you a short gap to switch from CAT's question style to the speed-heavy MBA CET format.</p>\n<p>Because the first attempt is compulsory under the note, do not plan to skip January and rely only on April. Treat the April attempt as a second chance to improve, not a substitute.</p>\n<p>The bigger change is for PGDM aspirants. If you are aiming for an AICTE-approved PGDM institute in Maharashtra, watch whether that institute now asks for an MAH CET score in its 2027 admission notice. Until the CET Cell publishes the information brochure, the exact admission rules for PGDM and PGCM seats are not known.</p>\n<p>Registration has not opened. Keep an eye on <a href=\"https://cetcell.mahacet.org/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">cetcell.mahacet.org</a> for the brochure and the registration window.</p>\n\n<h2>Important pointers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>18 Nov 2026:</strong> The first attempt of MAH MBA/MMS CET 2027 is scheduled for 28 to 30 January 2027, according to the State CET Cell's tentative schedule of 16 November 2026 (<a href=\"https://cetcell.mahacet.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/DATES-OF-COMMENCEMENT-OF-MAHA-CET-2027-16-NOV-2026.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">CET Cell press note</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>18 Nov 2026:</strong> The second attempt of MAH MBA/MMS CET 2027 is scheduled for 1 to 3 April 2027, and the press note calls it optional (<a href=\"https://cetcell.mahacet.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/DATES-OF-COMMENCEMENT-OF-MAHA-CET-2027-16-NOV-2026.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">CET Cell press note</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>18 Nov 2026:</strong> SNAP 2026 registration and payment close on 25 November 2026, and the three SNAP tests are on 13, 19 and 26 December 2026 (<a href=\"https://www.snaptest.org/snap-important-dates\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">snaptest.org</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>18 Nov 2026:</strong> XAT 2027 registration closes on 6 December 2026, and the exam is on 3 January 2027 from 2 pm to 5 pm (<a href=\"https://www.xatonline.in/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">xatonline.in</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>18 Nov 2026:</strong> The NMAT by GMAC 2026 testing window runs until 20 December 2026; registration and scheduling closed on 31 October 2026 (<a href=\"https://www.mba.com/exams/nmat\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">mba.com</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Preparing for CAT and MBA CET from Vidarbha? See our new city guide, <a href=\"top-cat-coaching-institutes-amravati-2026.html\">Top CAT Coaching Institutes in Amravati</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Last updated: 18 November 2026.</strong></p>\n"
